    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201852861976_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "System Technician Assistant-SW",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. System Technician Assistant-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 5 days ago Requisition ID: 1902 Apply Purpose/Objective of the Role: Assist the Systems technician with various hands-on duties. Tasks & Responsibilities: Including but not limited to: Replacing and repairing wireless hardware, telecommunications equipment Network device registration Digital signage management and installation Pulling wired networking cabling to repair or upgrade campus infrastructure Covering the help desk Supporting the media center with projector installation and configuration Answering phones, and responding to email/work requests Moderate ladder climbing will be required Qualifications: Willingness to learn new (and old) technology Being able to communicate effectively Lifting moderately heavy objects Familiarity with hand tools (drills, drywall saw etc.) Being able to work independently and with a partner Working knowledge of Windows,Mac and mobile device operating systems (linux experience is a bonus) Knowledge of home networking and wireless troubleshooting Knowledge of gaming consoles/smart devices NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Potential Future Career Benefit: Get lots of hands-on experience working with a variety of different technologies Learning how to troubleshoot infrastructure issues on an enterprise level Get an in-depth knowledge of modern networking, telecommunications, and digital signage systems Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Joe Peterson Commitment: Approximately 20 hours per week Academic Year: Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 Back Apply Copyright 