    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201849257915_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "P&G Research Assistant-SW",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. P&G Research Assistant-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 15 days ago Requisition ID: 1869 Apply Student Worker - Politics and Government Research Assistant Number of Openings: 2 Purpose/Objective of the Role: Research assistants will code human rights reports, continuing to build a global dataset on human rights abuses. Project is led by Professor Franklin, with support from a grant from the Centennial Center with the American Political Science Association. Tasks & Responsibilities : Research Assistants (RAs) will be trained on applying coding schemes to measure the severity and targets of human rights abuses. RAs will then use information in human rights reports to code the variables for a wide range of countries. RAs will largely work independently at times that fit their schedules but will meet regularly with Prof. Franklin and discuss any questions or difficulties they encounter in the coding process. The position could be fall only or extend into spring depending on how long the grant funding holds out. Qualifications/Skills: Current OWU student, sophomore status or higher, preferably majoring in Politics and Government, International Studies, or similar social science field. Students must be able to carefully follow directions, work independently and stay on task. Students must also attend meetings with professor and communicate any questions or difficulties. Potential Future Career Benefit: This position will be very useful to students considering graduate school. RAs will learn about social science research and they will also learn a lot about human rights around the world. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: James Franklin Commitment: 5-6 hours per week, minimum wage Term: Fall 26 - Spring 27 - temporary, part-time position Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label