      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Inorganic Chemistry Lab TA-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 16 days ago Requisition ID: 1862 Apply Purpose/Objective of the Role: Assist in the Inorganic Chemistry lab Tasks & Responsibilities: Prepare for every laboratory meeting by reading the laboratory experiment in the laboratory manual. You should understand every step of the procedure. Familiarize yourself with the pre-lab assignments such that you can help students with questions they may have about the assignment. If you have difficulty with #1 or #2, it is your responsibility to see the instructor before lab. You must come to lab prepared. Show up on time to perform your duties. Assist the laboratory instructor in duties directly related to the delivery of the lab. Receive laboratory safety training. See Dr. Grunkemeyer. Follow all safety guidelines; wear goggles and appropriate clothing. Circulate among the students in the laboratory section, helping students with questions as they have them. Watch students to be sure they are using proper technique. Correct them when they show poor technique. Do not just give students the answers. Lead them through the reasoning that will guide them to the right way of thinking about problems in lab. Make sure students have returned common equipment (such as centrifuges and glassware) to the proper location at the end of lab. Make sure students have cleaned up their work area at the end of lab. Qualifications: Applicants should have successfully completed one year of CHEM 260/261 before applying for this position. Potential Future Career Benefit: Peer leadership experience, insight into TA responsibilities in graduate school NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Heather Grunkemeyer Commitment: 3 hours per week, minimum wage Term: Full Academic Year Fall 2026 only, temporary, part-time position Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consen