      "title": "Communications Assistant-SW",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Communications Assistant-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 19 days ago Requisition ID: 1857 Apply Communications Assistant-SW 8 - Vacant positions Purpose/Objective of the Role: The student will assist in the operations of the OWU Sports Information department, primarily providing assistance with statistics during home athletics events. The student may also assist with day-to-day office work as well as other communications efforts for the department. Tasks & Responsibilities: Spotting and calling out plays as they happen during games, providing information on statistics and players involved Assisting with press box operations and statistics inputting Distributing statistics and other information to teams, officials, and media Assisting with the day-to-day operations of the OWU Sports Information department Qualifications/Skills: plays and communicate them clearly. The abilities to think quickly and be adaptable are helpful. General knowledge of sports and their differing rules and statistics is preferred. The student will be trained by staff for in-game operations. Potential Future Career Benefit : This job is a great starting point for a student who wants to pursue a career in sports or communications. The student will gain valuable experience within the inner-workings of college athletics and have the opportunity to develop connections with professionals in the field. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Brendan Eagan Commitment: Flexible (2-10) hours per week Term: Full Academic Year - (Fall26 - Spring 27) tempora