      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Communications Content Creator-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 19 days ago Requisition ID: 1856 Apply Communications Content Creator-SW 4 - Vacant positions Purpose/Objective of the Role: The student will assist the OWU Sports Information department in creating content for the OWU Athletics website and social media pages. Content will include (but is not limited to) photo galleries, videos, graphics, podcast, and written materials (e.g. game recaps, feature stories, etc.). Tasks & Responsibilities: Taking photos/videos during home games and other athletics events Creating short videos, reels, or graphics for social media Sorting and editing photos and videos for posting- writing game recaps, feature stories, and other materials for the OWU Athletics website Communicating with the Sports Information Director about deadlines for posting, content schedule, etc. Qualifications/Skills: Student photographers/videographers are preferred to have experience with capturing photos/video during athletics events and are preferred to have their own equipment and editing software. Student writers must have proficient writing skills; a general understanding of sports-writing as well as sports rules, trends, and statistics is helpful. Potential Future Career Benefit : This job is a great starting point for a student who wants to pursue a career in sports, communications, or content creation. The student will gain valuable experience within the inner-workings of college athletics and have the opportunity to develop connections with professionals in the field and get their work into the public eye. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Brendan Eagan Commitment: Flexible (2-10) hours per week Term: Full Academic Year - (Fall26 - Spring 27) temporary, part-time position Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below: Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label che