    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=a2082ac8-6363-4a1c-92d0-adacd9e4f844&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201845476096_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Lifeguard-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 27 days ago Requisition ID: 1838 Apply Lifeguard Position — Meek Aquatics Facility Purpose/Objective of the Role: Ohio Wesleyan University is seeking currently certified American Red Cross Lifeguards to support programming and aquatic activities at the Meek Aquatics Facility. Schedule: Hours vary throughout the week and may include the following shifts: Weekdays: 5:00–9:30 a.m., 12:00–2:00 p.m., 4:00–7:00 p.m., and 7:00–9:30 p.m. Saturdays: Varying hours based on scheduled swim meets and facility programming Sundays: 12:00–4:00 p.m. to support club swim team activities This position is an excellent opportunity for students who are currently certified by the American Red Cross as a Lifeguard and are interested in working in a dynamic aquatic facility environment. If you are interested in the position, please contact bjward@owu.edu for more information and to express your interest. Tasks & Responsibilities: Ensure the safety and well-being of all members, participants, and guests using the pool facility. Actively monitor the pool, surrounding deck areas, and aquatic activities at all times. Inspect and ensure the proper operation and readiness of lifeguarding and aquatic safety equipment. Conduct and accurately document daily pool chemical and water quality checks. Enforce all Athletic Department, facility, and pool safety policies and procedures. Respond promptly and appropriately to emergencies and follow established emergency action protocols. Qualifications: Current American Red Cross Lifeguard, CPR/AED and First Aid Training Certifications Potential Future Career Benefit: This position provides valuable experience in safety, leadership, communication, teamwork, and emergency response. The skills developed as a lifeguard can benefit students in a wide range of future careers, particularly those involving leadership, recreation, athletics, education, healthcare, public safety, and customer service. The position also provides an opportunity to build professionalism, responsibility, and confidence in a workplace environment. Application Instructions: NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Bethany Reed Commitment: Hours Vary Academic Year: Fall-26 & Spring 27 Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Fun