      "title": "Help Desk Assistant-SW",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Help Desk Assistant-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 27 days ago Requisition ID: 1837 Apply Help Desk Assistant-Student Worker Number of Openings: 7 Purpose/Objective of the Role: To provide telephone, email, webchat, and walk-up support, as well as keeps online support resources up-to-date. Technical Assistance and Support Answer Help Desk phone calls and web chat requests Answer email questions and requests for assistance that come in as tickets Assist with connecting devices to our campus networks Provide technical support to the campus community, using help resources provided Monitor email and web chat through online systems Check the status of online resources as needed Accurately escalate any unresolved problems to Information Services staff, according to documentation Keep the front lobby area clean and in acceptable condition Always enter the user’s name and contact info, along with the nature of their call Check voicemails that come in as Help Desk tickets Keep Information Services staff up-to-date on any concerns Keeping Documentation Up-to-Date Edit and revise the Oh-Wooo Help Desk website (helpdesk.owu.edu) and internal department resources as needed Keep an editorial eye on any pages used and update when needed Share helpful tips & tricks found with the team and staff Qualification/Skills Good communication, both written and oral Computer knowledge & troubleshooting (the more the better) Customer service (often more important than technical know-how) Initiative and ability to work independently Potential Future Career Benefit Develop and improve customer service skills and communication skills Exposure to and familiarity with both IT industry and higher education field Gain professional references NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: David Soliday Commitment: Approximately 8-10 hours per week Academic Year: Fall- 26 & Spring 27 Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filt