      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. RegiStar Student Guides-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 28 days ago Requisition ID: 1835 Apply RegiStar Student Guides-Student Worker Number of positions available: 8 Purpose/Objective of the Role: As a RegiStar Student Guide, you are the welcoming face and knowledgeable peer resource on behalf of the Registrar’s Office. Your primary focus is helping fellow students navigate registration, academic policies, Degree Audit, and the administrative practicalities of being a student via front-desk, phone, and email support. In addition to peer guidance, you will assist faculty, staff, alums, and visitors while supporting key administrative operations. Tasks & Responsibilities: Guide & Empower Peers: Serve as a frontline guide, helping your fellow students understand and resolve common issues related to registration, academic records, and graduation. Deliver Multi-Channel Service: Respond to inquiries warmly and accurately via front-desk walk-ins, phone calls, and email to direct students and other campus community members to the best resources to meet their needs. Contribute to a Seamless Experience: Assist with essential office tasks, such as reviewing documents and processing student requests, to ensure all administrative processes run smoothly for students. Collaborate on Special Projects: Contribute to initiatives that directly enhance the student experience, such as auditing web guides, testing new portal features, or researching campus needs. Qualifications/Skills: Compassion & Active Listening: A genuine desire to help peers navigate academic processes with patience and care. Clear Communication: Ability to translate complex policies and procedures in a simple, straightforward, and friendly way. Courtesy & Professionalism: Commitment to maintaining strict confidentiality regarding student records (FERPA compliance) while representing the University with integrity, maturity, and poise. Curiosity & Problem-Solving: A curious and proactive approach to understanding challenges and developing new solutions. Potential Future Career Benefit: This role offers hands-on experience in administrative operations, customer relationship management, and data privacy compliance. You will build highly marketable skills in peer mentorship, conflict resolution, and project coordination - ideal preparation for careers in higher education, management, human resources, or public administration. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Lee Richards Commitment: 3-9 hours per week, minimum wage Term: Full Academic Year (Fall & Spring), temporary, part-time position Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how 