      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Bishop Ambassadors-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 29 days ago Requisition ID: 1829 Apply Bishop Ambassadors ( Fall 26 - Spring 27 ) Number of Openings: 20 Various Roles: Event Ambassador Tour Guide Student Supervisor Admission Intern Purpose/Objective of the Role: The OWU Admission Office is seeking to fill multiple positions in the Admissions department. Only OWU students are eligible to apply and they must be in good academic standing. Most importantly, students should demonstrate a genuine enthusiasm for OWU and a strong desire to share that with various constituents (prospective students/families, school and independent counselors, etc.) The Bishop Ambassador program at OWU offers the opportunity to develop valuable leadership, communication, and public speaking skills while representing a prestigious university. Hours will vary by role. Weekend work will be required. Key Responsibilities: Conduct Campus Tours: Lead engaging and informative campus tours for prospective students and their families, showcasing the university's facilities, academic programs, student life, and key resources. Provide Information: Offer accurate and up-to-date information about the university’s offerings, admissions process, campus culture, and student support services in a clear and approachable manner. Represent the University: Serve as a positive and enthusiastic ambassador for the university, reflecting the institution’s values, mission, and culture. Engage Prospective Students: Foster connections with prospective students and their families by answering questions, addressing concerns, and sharing personal experiences related to campus life and academics. Assist with Events: Support the Office of Admission by assisting with special events, open houses, and information sessions, ensuring smooth operations and a welcoming atmosphere. Must be available to work on Saturdays. Collaborate with Admission Team: Work closely with the admissions staff to maintain consistency in the delivery of information and ensure a seamless experience for all visitors. This will include help with daily office functions such as mailings, event preparations, data entry, etc. Promote University Programs: Highlight various academic programs, extracurricular activities, student organizations, and campus resources to help prospective students make informed decisions. Provide Feedback: Collect feedback from visitors about their experience and share insights with the Admissions team to improve future tours and events. Maintain Professionalism: Exhibit professionalism at all times by adhering to the university’s dress code, punctuality standards, and communication protocols. Answer Admission Office Phone: Be the point person to answer phone calls to the Admissions Office and transfer calls appropriately. Other Duties as Assigned: Perform other related tasks as needed to support the Office of Admissions goals and ensure a positive experience. Desired skills: Must demonstrate a genuine enthusiasm for OWU and a strong desire to share that with various constituents. Must be outgoing and able to represent the Admission Office and Ohio Wesleyan in a positive and professional manner. Must exhibit strong written and verbal communication skills. Must be comfortable speaking in front of both large and small groups. Must show a commitment to providing a high level of customer service. Must be comfortable engaging with people of all ages, backgrounds and types. Must be capable of and willing to lead multiple tours in one day, if needed. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Abigail McMaster Hours per week : Varies Commitment: Part time Term: Fall 26 - Spring 27 Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
