      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Futurety Marketing Strategy Intern-SW Student Delaware, OH, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1817 Apply Purpose/Objective of the Role: Futurety is a digital analytics company, founded by a local serial entrepreneur. Futurety is seeking an OWU student intern to support branding, marketing strategy, and content development for a growing venture serving healthcare and local small–mid-sized businesses. The intern will help update core marketing materials, conduct competitor and market research, and build a practical content and social media strategy that the team can execute after the internship ends. Tasks & Responsibilities: Assist with updating slide decks, presentations, and other marketing materials to reflect current Futurety branding. Support clarification of Futurety’s value proposition for target segments (e.g., healthcare organizations, local Small to Medium Businesses (SMB). Conduct online competitor and market research and summarize key findings. Help design a social media content calendar and basic content strategy for Huckle. Produce clear, usable deliverables (updated decks, competitor research document, strategy summary, content calendar). Participate in regular coaching meetings with the OWU supervisor and check-ins with Futurety team members. Work independently between meetings, managing time around coursework while meeting agreed deadlines. Qualifications/Skills: Currently enrolled Ohio Wesleyan University student. Preferred class standing: junior or senior; strong sophomores considered. Coursework or experience in Marketing, Business & Economics, Digital Analytics, or related fields. Familiarity with basic marketing concepts (target markets, value propositions, content planning). Strong written communication and presentation/slide creation skills. Organized, reliable, and able to manage 10–15 hours per week around class commitments. Professional, comfortable collaborating with external partners in a business environment. Potential Future Career Benefit: Applied experience in branding, positioning, and marketing strategy for a real organization. Practice conducting competitor/market research and translating insights into recommendations. Experience designing content calendars and simple social media strategies. Portfolio-ready examples of strategy documents, updated decks, and content plans. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Molly Queen Commitment: 12 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position Fall 2026 only Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit o