      "title": "Student Worker - Biological Sciences Assistant",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Student Worker - Biological Sciences Assistant Student Delaware, OH, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1804 Apply Student Worker – Biological Sciences Assistant Number of Openings: 8 Purpose/Objective of the Role: You will be assisting the Biology Laboratory Coordinators and/or Greenhouse Manager Tasks & Responsibilities: Duties of the Biological Sciences Assistant can include: Helping to set up and break down Biology labs, washing labware, measuring liquid and dry media, restocking lab supplies, animal care, watering plants, testing eye wash stations, repairing equipment, cleaning field lab equipment, assisting StAP and/or Museum Interns with special projects, public science outreach programs, assisting faculty members during Biol 122 laboratory sections (if qualified), following health and safety guidelines. Animal care duties include: providing day to day support for the feeding and housing of departmental invertebrates and fish, checking/recording room temperature and humidity, cleaning fish tanks, making sure that filters, freezers, and refrigerators are operating correctly. Qualifications/Skills: Successful completion of the following courses (may be currently enrolled this semester): Biol 120 (Introduction to Cell Biology) Biol 122 (Organisms & Their Environment) Attention to detail Ability to work well independently and as part of a team Potential Future Career Benefit: Any field in the biological sciences NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions: Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Lisa Tabak Commitment: 3-6 hours per week Term: Full Academic Year (Fall 2026 & Spring 2027), temporary, part-time position Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
