      "title": "Student Worker - Floor Associate",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Student Worker - Floor Associate Student Delaware, OH, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1802 Apply Student Worker – Floor Associate Number of Openings: 16 Purpose/Objective of the Role: Welcome all to The 1842. Taking care of The 1842 by removing trash, cleaning up spills, setting up games/activities, and reporting problems that may arise. Tasks & Responsibilities : Provide welcoming atmosphere Empty trash and recycling cans when they become full Clean up spills of beverage and food Dispose of trash and wipe down tables in between uses Provide tv channel changes when requested Help in completing opening and closing tasks Once an hour bathroom and patio checks for tidiness Helping to set up, run, and tear down special events Report of equipment that is broken or not functioning as intended Report any actions or incidents that jeopardize student safety, damage property, or are unlawful that occur on the grounds of the facility Other duties as assigned Qualifications/Skills: Willingness to work with others Good communication skills Available to work nights and weekends Potential Future Career Benefit: Hospitality experience Working in group settings NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Anna Pellegrin Commitment: 5-20 hours per week Rate of pay is $11.00 an hour Term: Fall & Spring – (26/27) (temporary, part-time position) Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a