      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Student Worker - Education Student Delaware, OH, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1785 Apply Student Worker – Education Number of Openings: 3 Purpose/Objective of the Role: The Education Department is seeking a reliable, friendly, and organized student worker to assist the Education Department. This role offers an excellent opportunity to gain professional experience in a dynamic      academic environment. Tasks & Responsibilities: Greet any students/faculty/staff who enter the Education Department Work on projects with the Education Dept. Assist with event planning and coordination, including preparing materials and setting up rooms. Run errands and jobs as assigned Support departmental projects and perform other administrative tasks as assigned. Qualifications: Must be a current student, preferably enrolled in the Education program. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and comfortable learning new software. Experience with Canva created a Plus Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Dependable, punctual, and able to work independently as well as part of a team. Previous office or customer service experience is a plus, but not required. Potential Future Career Benefit: This role offers an excellent opportunity to gain professional experience in a dynamic academic environment especially for an Education student. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Christina Muirhead-Gould Commitment: Part Time ( about 20 hours total with all student workers ) Term: Fall 26 & Spring 27 Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below. Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
