      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Recruitment Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Student Worker - Bishop Scholars Tutor Student Delaware, OH, US 30+ days ago Requisition ID: 1771 Apply Purpose/Objective of the Role: The Bishop Scholars Program seeks energized and committed students to tutor elementary youth in Delaware City Schools, Columbus City Schools, and Columbus Bilingual Academy North for the fall, 2026 and spring, 2027 semesters. Tutoring days include Monday,Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday with various tutoring times from approximately 8:15 a.m.– 4:00 p.m. This is a PAID position and all potential tutors must complete an in-person interview, criminal background check, and mandatory training prior to being accepted into the program. Transportation to and from our partnering schools will be provided. Tasks & Responsibilities: Must commit to the full semester! Attend assigned day(s) of tutoring. Be on time! University transportation will leave at designated time. We will not wait for you. Wear appropriate dress attire, as outlined by OWU and our partner school guidelines. Must wear a Bishop Scholars or OWU branded shirt. Meet with assigned elementary students each scheduled day and actively interact & tutor in core competencies outlined by the partner school (Math and Reading, primarily). Complete student tutor logs each assigned day of tutoring. Communicate attendance or program concerns to the Bishop Scholars Director at least two (2) hours prior to campus departure . Actively participate in on-campus training(s) and Lunch-and-Learns. Share the mission and work of the Bishop Scholars Program with peers in the campus community. Represent the Bishop Scholars Program on campus at Connection Conferences, symposiums, and recruitment events. Participate in and complete program surveys and reflections. Work hours must be entered into ADP on your assigned tutoring day. Qualifications: Excellent Communication Skills Time Management Skills Effective Written skills Unwavering Commitment to Attendance Strong team player with the ability to adapt to diverse team/school participants Passion for working with children and fostering a positive learning environment Spanish Speaking (preferred for one partner school, but not required) Federal Work Study Recipient (preferred, not required) Potential Future Career Benefit: The Bishop Scholars Program provides excellent experience for students interested in the Education, Medical, or any field that requires working with the public by enhancing communication, written and interpersonal skills. Experience will include working with both children and professional staff. NOTE: Employment sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States. Application Instructions : Complete the ADP application by selecting \"Apply\" button and answer all questions. Supervisor: Kerri Robe Commitment: 3-8 hours per week Term: temporary, part-time position ( Fall 2026 & Spring 2027 ) Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to hel